{"event_type":"review","id":"899cff93c770e74d3d7ec07e8dd0fc65eda21bc441bca6e88c363c64b29ea4d9","occurred_at":"2026-11-07T22:03:27Z","payload":{"artifacts":[{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/e9f7ea515e882ae1017075956295b922d8b3b709da95abfdd5a75272c23eb32f","sha256":"e9f7ea515e882ae1017075956295b922d8b3b709da95abfdd5a75272c23eb32f"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/6d3cdcdd914b4577dcb0bd57c36d99a8bfb255394569c4159669b6defa1fd96b","sha256":"6d3cdcdd914b4577dcb0bd57c36d99a8bfb255394569c4159669b6defa1fd96b"},{"kind":"git-bundle","location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/e6dee95054b80d7856595cf537106efbc357ab72251e4645fa6b70b3542ec2b5","sha256":"e6dee95054b80d7856595cf537106efbc357ab72251e4645fa6b70b3542ec2b5"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/09c92da07f292962bec3710632bd7f34ed0e74974725ee8619fdc7d61b006cb8","sha256":"09c92da07f292962bec3710632bd7f34ed0e74974725ee8619fdc7d61b006cb8"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/8a955fc8073c0a8819a7525feb1a55f444fa9bf892232a873b587d27834bd802","sha256":"8a955fc8073c0a8819a7525feb1a55f444fa9bf892232a873b587d27834bd802"}],"attempt_id":"622ca1c95f82fdd00a789814115cdc956854bc16285dbad017bbb6f34b3f8780:0:1","base":"2f2e27c14cf7a2e76f677ea3ced6d0e9d8af3457","completion":{"errors":[],"exit_code":0,"scope_verified":true,"skipped":false,"terminal":true},"findings":[{"anchor_status":"unverified","blob":"52ba9c56f4799da5ef9bd98206229ca41f2b0821","body":"**Hash the input snapshot, not the original input.**\n\nIf a plain object has an accessor, validation, `structuredClone`, and `hashInputs` can read different values from it. For example, an accessor that returns `1` twice and then `2` stores `1` at Line 130 but hashes `2` here. This change adds the first read during validation. Capture one snapshot, validate that snapshot, and hash that same snapshot. ([html.spec.whatwg.org](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/structured-data.html))","id":"ec188a7705e86962d871ae991258b8277cd3e3a1654b574231ba58f4c57b2ad0","intervals":[],"path":"src/kernel/manifest.ts","severity":"major","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Hash the input snapshot, not the original input."},{"anchor_status":"unverified","blob":"52ba9c56f4799da5ef9bd98206229ca41f2b0821","body":"**Make sparse-array snapshots match their hash.**\n\n`new Array(1)` and `[null]` now hash identically. `structuredClone` preserves the hole, so an op can distinguish the dispatched inputs with `0 in input`. A resumed job can therefore reuse a result for a different input. Normalize holes to `null` in the snapshot, or reject sparse arrays before hashing. ([html.spec.whatwg.org](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/structured-data.html))","id":"8155f2ac32f3aa83fd5097c2c780f334adf736be0de1fdec93bc15ca040510a3","intervals":[],"path":"src/kernel/manifest.ts","severity":"major","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Make sparse-array snapshots match their hash."},{"anchor_status":"unverified","blob":"52ba9c56f4799da5ef9bd98206229ca41f2b0821","body":"**Reject array properties that the hash omits.**\n\nIn `src/kernel/manifest.ts:97`, arrays with enumerable non-index properties pass validation. `structuredClone` retains those properties, but `canonicalJson` omits them. If an input schema preserves such a property, resume can reuse a result for a different input. Reject non-index array properties before cloning.","id":"2827059ead340cbdad64af556d3d04450f359dcf41b0be808fb8a8f08a3428a3","intervals":[],"path":"src/kernel/manifest.ts","severity":"minor","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Reject array properties that the hash omits."}],"head":"70feeb7766b857940c4394e8a684daf7eacb3b93","head_tree":"067d49da10942551a3c39da201ad1d79467f9afa","input_scope":[{"blob":"52ba9c56f4799da5ef9bd98206229ca41f2b0821","intervals":[[52,58],[78,110],[118,120],[125,134]],"path":"src/kernel/manifest.ts"}],"job_id":"622ca1c95f82fdd00a789814115cdc956854bc16285dbad017bbb6f34b3f8780:0","outcome":"completed","paths":[{"baseline":{"entry":{"blob":"979960ef4c67d878716b1f41a8215d8d04b82a15","kind":"blob","mode":"100644","path":"src/kernel/manifest.ts"},"merge":"e24ac1dc85b2ed282b65a61219a39bb42b9015e7","method":"pre-merge","pre":"f1ed5ff42119584bca836d5182bd9d1d7f6edd5a","source_path":"src/kernel/manifest.ts"},"blob":"52ba9c56f4799da5ef9bd98206229ca41f2b0821","disposition":"included","mode":"100644","path":"src/kernel/manifest.ts","reason":"bounded verified input"}],"policy_digest":"eacd1bcf42a0e72eca72fcf9c1e9c8f97e7c515cd67a8fa7965c966924647693","repo":"camerontaylor/cq-toolkit","requested_scope":[{"blob":"52ba9c56f4799da5ef9bd98206229ca41f2b0821","intervals":[[78,110],[118,120],[125,134]],"path":"src/kernel/manifest.ts"}],"reviewed_scope":[{"blob":"52ba9c56f4799da5ef9bd98206229ca41f2b0821","intervals":[[78,110],[118,120],[125,134]],"path":"src/kernel/manifest.ts"}],"scope_digest":"72eca2c8dfe096a2213d984ccd8244685702eed924d863532543e5e0a8106160","source":{"authenticated":true,"id":"backfill-622ca1c95f82fdd00a789814115cdc956854bc16285dbad017bbb6f34b3f8780-g0-20261107T220031Z","producer":"crq-runner-app","repo":"camerontaylor/cq-toolkit","type":"crq-run"},"subject_id":"622ca1c95f82fdd00a789814115cdc956854bc16285dbad017bbb6f34b3f8780","target":"9ba0d4661956d91e3c1bd4a95ee9369044eaa9f3","target_tree":"067d49da10942551a3c39da201ad1d79467f9afa"},"schema":"cq.review-ledger/v1","source_key":"camerontaylor/cq-toolkit:crq-runner-app:backfill-622ca1c95f82fdd00a789814115cdc956854bc16285dbad017bbb6f34b3f8780-g0-20261107T220031Z"}